   "id": "intro-logging",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Logging Estructurado\n",
    "\n",
    "Módulo logging de Python, logs JSON, niveles de log"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "intro-section",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Introducción\n",
    "\n",
    "Un log estructurado permite buscar campos consistentes como nivel, servicio y request_id. A diferencia de logs de texto plano, los logs JSON son parseables y queryables por herramientas como Elasticsearch o Splunk.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Objetivos de Aprendizaje\n",
    "\n",
    "- Entender la ventaja de un log estructurado\n",
    "- Usar el módulo logging de Python correctamente\n",
    "- Configurar logs en formato JSON\n",
    "- Implementar correlación de requests con request_id\n",
    "- Definir y usar niveles de log apropiadamente"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "structured-logging-advantage",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Qué ventaja tiene un log estructurado\n",
    "\n",
    "> Un log estructurado permite buscar y filtrar por campos consistentes (nivel, servicio, request_id). Esto hace posible responder preguntas como: \"muéstrame todos los errores del servicio auth del último minuto\" de forma eficiente."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "structured-logging-code",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import json\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"=== Log Estructurado ===\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\"\"\n",
    "LOG DE TEXTO PLANO (difícil de buscar):\n",
    "  2024-01-15 10:23:45 ERROR Fallo en conexión a DB\n",
    "  2024-01-15 10:23:46 WARNING Retry attempt 1\n",
    "  2024-01-15 10:23:47 ERROR Fallo en conexión a DB\n",
    "\n",
    "LOG ESTRUCTURADO JSON (fácil de buscar):\n",
    "\"\"\")\n",
    "\n",
    "log_json = {\n",
    "    \"timestamp": \"2024-01-15T10:23:45Z\",\n",
    "    \"level\": \"ERROR\",\n",
    "    \"service\": \"auth-service\",\n",
    "    \"request_id\": \"abc-123-def\",\n",
    "    \"message\": \"Fallo en conexión a DB\",\n",
    "    \"error_code\": \"DB_CONN_001\",\n",
    "    \"host\": \"server-02\"\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "print(json.dumps(log_json, indent=2))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\"\"\n",
    "Búsquedas posibles con log estructurado:\n",
    "  - level=ERROR AND service=auth-service\n",
    "  - request_id=abc-123-def (todas las entradas de un request)\n",
    "  - timestamp>[2024-01-15T10:23:00Z] AND timestamp<[2024-01-15T10:24:00Z]\n",
    "\n",
    "Esto NO es posible con logs de texto plano.\n",
    "\"\"\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "python-logging-module",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Módulo logging de Python\n",
    "\n",
    "> El módulo logging de Python es el estándar para registrar eventos. Permite diferentes niveles, handlers, y formatters. Es preferible sobre print() porque es más controlable y configurable."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "logging-module-code",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import logging\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"=== Módulo logging de Python ===\")\n",
    "\n",
    "logging.basicConfig(\n",
    "    level=logging.INFO,\n",
    "    format='%(asctime)s - %(name)s - %(levelname)s - %(message)s'\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "logger = logging.getLogger('mi_servicio')\n",
    "\n",
    "logger.debug(\"Debug: variable x = %s\", 10)\n",
    "logger.info(\"Info: Solicitud recibida\")\n",
    "logger.warning(\"Warning: Conexión lenta\")\n",
    "logger.error(\"Error: Fallo en autenticación\")\n",
    "logger.critical(\"Critical: Base de datos inaccesible\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\"\"\n",
    "Niveles de log (de menor a mayor severidad):\n",
    "  DEBUG:    Información detallada de debug (desarrollo)\n",
    "  INFO:     Eventos normales (requests, operaciones)\n",
    "  WARNING:  Situaciones inesperadas pero no críticas\n",
    "  ERROR:    Errores que permiten continuar funcionando\n",
    "  CRITICAL: Fallos graves que paran la aplicación\n",
    "\"\"\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "json-formatter",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Logs en Formato JSON\n",
    "\n",
    "> Un JsonFormatter convierte cada log en una línea JSON. Esto permite que herramientas de observabilidad (ELK, Datadog, Splunk) indexen y busquen los logs eficientemente."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "json-formatter-code",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import logging\n",
    "import json\n",
    "from datetime import datetime\n",
    "\n",
    "class JsonFormatter(logging.Formatter):\n",
    "    def format(self, record):\n",
    "        log_obj = {\n",
    "            \"timestamp\": datetime.utcnow().isoformat() + \"Z\",\n",
    "            \"level\": record.levelname,\n",
    "            \"logger\": record.name,\n",
    "            \"message\": record.getMessage(),\n",
    "            \"module\": record.module,\n",
    "            \"function\": record.funcName,\n",
    "            \"line\": record.lineno,\n",
    "        }\n",
    "        if hasattr(record, 'request_id'):\n",
    "            log_obj['request_id'] = record.request_id\n",
    "        if record.exc_info:\n",
    "            log_obj['exception'] = self.formatException(record.exc_info)\n",
    "        return json.dumps(log_obj)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "handler = logging.StreamHandler()\n",
    "handler.setFormatter(JsonFormatter())\n",
    "logger = logging.getLogger('api')\n",
    "logger.setLevel(logging.INFO)\n",
    "logger.addHandler(handler)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Ejemplo de log JSON generado:\")\n",
    "logger.info(\"Solicitud recibida\")\n",
    "logger.error(\"Fallo en autenticación\", extra={\"request_id\": \"req-456\"})"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "request-correlation",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Correlación de Requests con request_id\n",
    "\n",
    "> El request_id permite seguir una solicitud a través de todos los servicios y logs. Cuando un request entra al sistema, se genera o extrae un ID único que se pasa a todos los componentes."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "correlation-code",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import uuid\n",
    "import logging\n",
    "import json\n",
    "\n",
    "class RequestContextFilter(logging.Filter):\n",
    "    def __init__(self):\n",
    "        super().__init__()\n",
    "        self.request_id = None\n",
    "    \n",
    "    def filter(self, record):\n",
    "        record.request_id = self.request_id or \"no-request-id\"\n",
    "        return True\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"=== Correlación de Requests ===\")\n",
    "\n",
    "def process_request(request_id=None):\n",
    "    request_id = request_id or str(uuid.uuid4())\n",
    "    \n",
    "    logger = logging.getLogger('api')\n",
    "    logger.info(f\"Request iniciado\", extra={'request_id': request_id})\n",
    "    \n",
    "    logger.info(f\"Validando credenciales\", extra={'request_id': request_id})\n",
    "    auth_result = validate_credentials()\n",
    "    \n",
    "    logger.info(f\"Consultando base de datos\", extra={'request_id': request_id})\n",
    "    data = query_db()\n",
    "    \n",
    "    logger.info(f\"Request completado\", extra={'request_id': request_id})\n",
    "    return {\"status\": \"ok\", \"request_id\": request_id}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def validate_credentials():\n",
    "    return True\n",
    "\n",
    "def query_db():\n",
    "    return [{\"id\": 1, \"name\": \"producto1\"}]\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "result = process_request()\n",
    "print(f\"\\nRequest ID generado: {result['request_id']}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\"\"\n",
    "Con request_id puedes buscar en Elasticsearch:\n",
    "  request_id: \"abc-123-def\" AND level: ERROR\n",
    "\n",
    "Esto muestra todos los errores relacionados con ese request\n",
    "específico, útil para debugging distribuido.\n",
    "\"\"\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "log-levels-best-practices",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Niveles de Log: Mejores Prácticas\n",
    "\n",
    "> Usar el nivel de log correcto facilita el filtrado y reduce ruido. DEBUG para desarrollo, INFO para operaciones normales, WARNING para situaciones anómalas, ERROR para fallos en operaciones específicas."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "log-levels-code",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"=== Niveles de Log: Cuándo Usar Cada Uno ===\")\n",
    "\n",
    "niveles = {\n",
    "    \"DEBUG\": [\n",
    "        \"Variables de entrada/salida\",\n",
    "        \"Decisiones de lógica de negocio\",\n",
    "        \"Llamadas a funciones externas\",\n",
    "        \"Detalles de loops e iteraciones\",\n",
    "    ],\n",
    "    \"INFO\": [\n",
    "        \"Request HTTP recibido\",\n",
    "        \"Operación completada exitosamente\",\n",
    "        \"Inicio/parada de servicio\",\n",
    "        \"Transiciones de estado importantes\",\n",
    "    ],\n",
    "    \"WARNING\": [\n",
    "        \"Retry de operación\",\n",
    "        \"Datos de entrada no válidos (sanearizados)\",\n",
    "        \"Recursos cercanos al límite\",\n",
    "        \"Autenticación fallida (intento)\",\n",
    "    ],\n",
    "    \"ERROR\": [\n",
    "        \"Excepción capturada y manejada\",\n",
    "        \"Fallo en operación específica\",\n",
    "        \"Timeout en llamada externa\",\n",
    "    ],\n",
    "    \"CRITICAL\": [\n",
    "        \"Base de datos inaccesible\",\n",
    "        \"Fallo de autenticación del sistema\",\n",
    "        \"Memoria agotada\",\n",
    "    ],\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "for nivel, ejemplos in niveles.items():\n",
    "    print(f\"\\n{nivel}:\")\n",
    "    for ejemplo in ejemplos:\n",
    "        print(f\"  - {ejemplo}\")"
   ]
  },
